language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Farmer and cows: distribute cows numbered 1 to num_cows among the sons so that each son gets the given number of cows and every son gets the same total milk (a cow gives milk equal to its number).
given num_cows : int
given num_sons : int
$ the number of cows each son must receive, one entry per son
given cows_per_son : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_sons)] of int
$ gives[s,i] is true when son s receives cow i
find gives : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_sons), int(1..num_cows)] of bool
$ cow_assignments[i] is the son (0-based) that receives cow i, read off from gives
find cow_assignments : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_cows)] of int(0..num_sons-1)
$ milk_each is the total milk each son receives
find milk_each : int(0..num_cows * (num_cows + 1) / 2)
branching on [gives]
such that
$ the milk of all cows, 1 + 2 + ... + num_cows, is shared equally among the sons
milk_each * num_sons = num_cows * (num_cows + 1) / 2,
$ the son of each cow is the one whose entry in gives is true
forAll i : int(1..num_cows) . (cow_assignments[i] = (sum s : int(1..num_sons) . toInt(gives[s,i]) * (s - 1))),
$ every cow goes to exactly one son
forAll i : int(1..num_cows) . ((sum s : int(1..num_sons) . toInt(gives[s,i])) = 1),
$ each son receives exactly the number of cows given for him
forAll s : int(1..num_sons) . ((sum i : int(1..num_cows) . toInt(gives[s,i])) = cows_per_son[s]),
$ each son's cows give him exactly milk_each litres of milk in total, the milk of a cow being its number
forAll s : int(1..num_sons) . ((sum i : int(1..num_cows) . toInt(gives[s,i]) * i) = milk_each)
